  "configuration_id": "config_014",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted (config_007, acc=0.7062) dramatically outperforms all other tested configurations, with the RNA encoder choice (scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000 >> scgpt) being the dominant factor. However, we have only tested imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder with scvi_n200. Config_014 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted) keeps the proven-best aggregation (avgpool) and fusion (weighted) while testing whether a different image encoder could further improve or at least match the current best. This is the best use of experiment 7 because: (1) it isolates the image encoder axis with all other parameters at their known-optimal values, (2) it reduces uncertainty about whether the 0.7062 result is specific to imagenet_vit_l or generalizable, and (3) with 3 experiments remaining, confirming or refuting the image encoder choice will guide whether to exploit the current best or explore alternative combinations in the final experiments."
}

